From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/24] ASoC: samsung: gts28-wm1814 machine driver for the
 SM-T715

Sound card of the Galaxy Tab S2 8.0 LTE: I2S0 with the WM1814 codec,
driven by the mainline WM8998 driver, as clock master.  MCLK1 is the PMU
CLKOUT on the 24 MHz oscillator; FLL1 makes SYSCLK = 49.152 MHz from it
while the codec is out of BIAS_OFF, and AIF1 runs from SYSCLK, as the
vendor pacific_arizona.c does.  DAPM pin switches for the speaker, the
headphones and the main microphone; the earpiece, the other
microphones, HDMI and jack detection are left out.

Checked on the SM-T715: "WM1814 revision B", card wm1814, and a 1 kHz
tone played on the speaker is picked up by the main microphone
(Goertzel 678.9 at 1 kHz against 0.1 at 500 and 1500 Hz).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
